==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*3 [[Ginger Snache]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Grand Emperor Warumongar]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**5 [[Madam Peng]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
**1 [[Baron Face]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Countess Koryessa]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
**2 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You want high level [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] for this stage, specifically [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]], [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]], and [[Ribbon Cat (Special Cat)|Pink Nyanko Ranger]], as they benefit the most from the survivability. You can easily build up a max wallet by slowly picking off every single peon at the start using a single [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] with [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cats]] as meatshields. Once you're ready to move on, you can summon [[Giga-Nyan Rex (Uber Rare Cat)|Giga-Nyan Prime DX]] and hit the enemy base to get the show on the road.

Yellow Nyanko Ranger and Green Nyanko Ranger do a very good job at holding the Kaijin off, and you'll want to keep stalling until Countess Koryessa spawns. Carefully time Talented [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to chunk her: the best opportunity is right after Great Emperor Warumongar attacks. As long as you can get a few good hits on her, you can finish her off later on with a second Giga-Nyan after the first one dies. Killing either Baron Face or Countess Koryessa can be considered a win condition, as they lose considerable pushing power, which usually leads to the other one dying thereafter. Because of this, you should prioritize chipping both with constant [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cats]] and Can Can Cats. The stage is very long, leaving plenty of room for error, to the point where stalling for a second Awakened Bahamut Cat isn't very difficult if everything goes downhill. The main thing to look out for is cash, since, while plentiful, it can get eaten up at an alarming rate if you're not mindful.

Cleanup poses no issue when it's just Great Emperor Warumongar all by himself. He reigns his army of evil henchmen no longer, and a boss without his associates is nothing more than a larper. Restore peace; finish the job.

